      <slug></slug>
      <title>coreboot board porting</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Coreboot</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You don&amp;#39;t like your BIOS? Want coreboot instead? Here is my story...&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk introduces some strategies for porting coreboot to new hardware. We go over the information gathering stage, data-mining, datasheet usage and common gotchas. The porting of a new motherboard but with existing chipset support, as well as kick-starting a new chipset port, are explained.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="411">Rudolf Marek</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>